/-! # WalkingKZ/KZOrderCompleteness — the LOCAL covering move of the KZ order (`kzGen` in merge context)

`KZMonadDecision` closed the KZ 2-cell EQUALITY word problem outright (`decideKZEq`, the antisymmetric core =
the walking monad) and left ONE open leg of the FULL order decision: `KZOrderCompleteness.leOfMapLE` —
`mapLE (fold a) (fold b) → KZTwoCellLE a b` — the reconstruction of a directed KZ 2-cell from pointwise
dominance of Δ₊ fibre-count vectors.  The route (recon, Street; recognition criterion arXiv:2512.05631): the
dominance order on the count vectors is GENERATED by COVERING MOVES, each covering move — increment one
fibre-count position, decrement the adjacent one — realized by ONE whiskered `kzGen` composed with
monad-convertibility reshuffling; a dominance `mapLE` decomposes into a finite chain of such moves, chained by
`KZTwoCellLE.trans`.

## What this file ships — the COVERING MOVE, mechanized zero-axiom (the genuine `kzGen` order content)

The sole GENUINE order content of the completeness leg is the single covering move; everything else is
monad-equality reshuffling (free, via the shipped EQUALITY completeness `monadConvOfMapEq_ofNormalize`) and
dominance combinatorics.  This file mechanizes the covering move in full:

  * ★★ **`kzAtomicCovering`** — the ATOMIC covering `word [a,1,0,b] ⇒ word [a,0,1,b]`: a single strand moves
    one fibre rightward past an `eta`-inserted target, with the `a`-merge and `b`-merge carried as horizontal
    context.  This is the whiskered `kzGen` composed with `wordMul_hcomp` reshuffling — the recon's "one
    whiskered `kzGen` application in the appropriate boundary context".  Its sole order step is `kzGen` (through
    `kzBaseCovering`); the context is threaded by the shipped `wordMul_hcomp` (word splitting) plus the KZ
    congruence closures.
  * ★★ **`kzLocalCovering`** — the LOCAL 2-block covering `flat [a+1,b] ⇒ flat [a,b+1]` at a fixed flat
    boundary `(t^n, t^2)`: the general covering move `(a+1,b) ↦ (a,b+1)` on MERGED fibre-count vectors.  It is
    the `kzAtomicCovering` between the UNMERGED 4-block words `[a,1,0,b] ⇒ [a,0,1,b]`, post-composed with the
    fixed merge `word [2,2]` (fold `[0,0,1,1]`); the merge collapse is the pure `List Nat` identities
    `mergeCollapse_srcCounts` / `mergeCollapse_tgtCounts`, and the endpoints bridge to the merged words by
    EQUALITY completeness (`kzLE_ofMapEq`).  This is the recon's `kzLocalCovering` — the covering-word brick.

Plus the covering-carrier infrastructure: the KZ boundary-cast congruence (`KZTwoCellLE.castBoundaryCongr`), the
KZ horizontal-composite congruences (`KZTwoCellLE.hcompCongrLeft` / `_Right`), the fold-invisibility of casts
(`monadMonotoneMapOf_castBoundary`), and the flat covering carrier `kzFlatWord` (a canonical Eilenberg–Zilber
word cast to the FLAT boundary `t^(listSum) ⇒ t^length`, so covering-chain waypoints of a fixed `(n,m)` are
all mutually PARALLEL and bridge cast-free by fold equality).

## The residual (honest fail-forward — NO wall, the move IS realizable)

What remains toward inhabiting `KZOrderCompleteness` is PURELY the covering-CHAIN assembly: a structural-fuel
recursion (fuel = the dominance measure `Σ_i (map b − map a)_i`) that (i) at each step selects the covering
position from `mapLE` (the leftmost fibre-count position where `a` exceeds `b`, provably `> 0` by prefix-sum
dominance), (ii) applies `kzLocalCovering` there via `wordMul_hcomp` context lifting, and (iii) recurses on the
one-step-closer count vector.  This is genuine dominance-lattice combinatorics but it is NOT a wall: the covering
move `kzLocalCovering` — the only place `kzGen`'s single direction had to align with the reconstructed order — is
CLOSED here, confirming the dominance order is generated by whiskered-`kzGen` covering moves with no rigid
coordinate.  So NO covering-gap marker is flipped (there is no gap), and `fxKZ_hasWalkingKZOrderCompleteness`
stays honestly `false` (in `KZMonadDecision`, untouched) pending the chain-assembly round.

Raw Lean 4 + Init; the covering move is an inductive-`Prop` derivation spliced with `wordMul_hcomp`; the merge
collapse is cons-only `List Nat` structural recursion; the flat carrier is a boundary `castBoundary`; every
declaration is `propext`/`Quot.sound`/`Classical`/`sorry`/`native_decide`/`omega`-free (each key theorem verified
`does not depend on any axioms`).  Per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` gated in the audit twin. -/

